# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole A3: the same `.get()`-chain read + `&`
# writer conflict, but rooted in a module-level `static` instead of a local.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then AddressSanitizer heap-use-after-free in `gorget_string_copy_cow`.
# `check_call_aliasing`'s participant filter admits only `DefKind::Variable`
# roots, and module globals resolve as `Static` — so a byte-identical program
# rejects when the collection is a local and is silently accepted when it is a
# global. That asymmetry is the tell: the check is spelled over syntax, not
# over places.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict`, exactly as the local
# spelling already is.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): OUT OF SUBSET — "item kind static is
# outside the phase-0 subset". Pinned against the ratified D10 exclusivity
# ruling rather than against a third implementation; recorded explicitly per
# Core #9. Full oracle note in `sound_excl_getchain_local.gg`.
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry, hole #3.
static Vector[String] G = Vector[String]()

void f(String s, Vector[String] &v):
    int i = 0
    while i < 4096:
        v.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
        i = i + 1
    print(s)

void main():
    G.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    f(G.get(0).unwrap(), &G)
